522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Deep within the ruins of the Galactic Core, silence echoes through the broken halls. The great engines that once pulsed with cosmic energy now lie dormant. Entire star systems wait in darkness, their survival depending on a single spark of power.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Legends speak of two ancient energy cells hidden within the chamber. One still brims with life, glowing faintly with the remnants of stored starlight. The other, however, has long since faded an empty husk, drained by time and corruption. Only the true, charged cell can awaken the Core once more. \(Appendix 7\))
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (But the challenge is not as simple as retrieval. The cells are scattered across different paths, and only one carries the vital charge. Your robot, acting as the lone guardian, must search the arena and identify the living cell. Weight of the both cells will be around 80g and the surface of both cells will be Blue. The discovery must be clear and decisive signaled through a buzzer, a flashing light, or another unmistakable mark of recognition.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5 6 7]
>>
endobj
