712 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1301 0 R
/E (All robots will be evaluated on their ability to complete the five designated tasks autonomously within the given arena. Evaluation will consider not only task completion but also accuracy, stability, and compliance with the specified rules. Judges will closely observe task execution to ensure that actions such as cube placement, button actuation, color detection, wall-following, ball throwing, and energy cell handling are performed strictly by the robot without external assistance.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
713 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1302 0 R
/E (Robots will be assessed on technical performance \(precision of movements, reliability of sensors, and successful execution of computations\), arena compatibility \(safe interaction with surfaces, ramps, and walls\), and design compliance \(size, weight, and power restrictions\). Any robot that causes deliberate damage to the arena, bypasses tasks, or violates physical or operational constraints will be penalized or disqualified.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
714 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1303 0 R
/E (Scoring will be strictly based on the official marking scheme, with deductions applied for errors, collisions, missed objectives, or violations. Partial points may be awarded for incomplete task execution if the robot demonstrates progress toward the objective. Judges will also verify that recorded binary values, matrix calculations, and final placements are correct as per the rules.All evaluations will be carried out by the competition officials, and their decisions are final and binding.)
/Pg 37 0 R
>>
endobj
